          <div style="text-indent:20pt; margin-top:6pt; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;"><font style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Potential benefits exist in the Master Fund&#8217;s </font><font style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">investments in </font><font style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">the current interest rate environment.</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  With an improving economy tend to come rising interest rates and the Master Fund&#8217;s investment strategy that focuses on originating floating rate loans  and financing these investments with floating rate liabilities allows the Master Fund to benefit especially relative to investment vehicles that focus on fixed rate loans. Quantitative easing by the Federal Reserve and maintenance of historically low interest rates have contributed to economic recovery, corporate stability and decreased unemployment, leading to increased corporate strength and rental growth. The Master Fund intends to predominantly make CRE debt investments with a coupon consisting of a credit spread over a floating rate index, usually LIBOR. As interest rates rise, the interest income produced by floating rate investments will also increase, producing more revenue. The Master Fund also intends to finance or match its floating rate assets with floating rate borrowings. Since the Master Fund only finances a portion of any given investment to generate improved returns, the benefits of rising interest rates to the Master Fund&#8217;s floating rate investments will outpace the increasing cost of its borrowings, resulting in corresponding improved returns on its invested equity. Additionally, for other investments, including the Master Fund&#8217;s CRE equity investments, it generally plans to secure long-term, fixed rate financing. In today&#8217;s current low interest rate environment, the Advisors believe the Master Fund&#8217;s ability to take advantage of low-cost financing opportunities will produce higher returns on its investments over time. We believe the current period of historically low interest rates and an improving economy supports a rising interest rate environment, which may benefit the Master Fund&#8217;s investment strategy and our Shareholders. </div>
